 "vanilla_note": "dac DOES have a vanilla formatter: the `formatter is None` branch of `serve.py:608-617` and `run_eval.py:300-309`, which fills `template_text.format(context=..., question=...)` into one user turn under `DEFAULT_SYSTEM_INSTRUCTION`. The vanilla rows here carry no `reference_*` fields because that branch was not driven when this file was recorded, not because it does not exist. One recorded delta, unchanged and not a defect: dattn normalises an empty or whitespace-only context to `<empty_context>` (`prompt/segment.py:33-38`) and dac passes `raw_context` through, so on the `empty` case the dattn prompt is 5 tokens longer than dac's, 228 vs 223 on Qwen/Qwen3.6-27B. Re-measured at 221 vs 216 with an empty question string, the same +5. Every non-empty context renders byte-identically because `normalize_context` returns it unchanged. review MINOR 46. The system turn is a separate recorded delta, docs/PROVENANCE.md P11.",
 "known_deltas": {
  "first_span_lead": "google/gemma-4-31B-it chunk_multi_turn_tool only: dattn's first segment span starts 3 tokens earlier than dac's, because dattn keeps the <|turn>model header with the pair it opens while dac's per-family regex starts at <|tool_call>. F D1, low severity.",
  "d2_truncation": "collision_qwen and collision_gemma: dac's per-family regex ends the affected segment span at the injected markup instead of the real turn boundary, with no error reported (30 tokens on Qwen3.6, 424 on Gemma 4 here; over 2000 when the quote lands early in a segment body). collision_pair is the other path and is NOT silent: a forged tool-call pair makes dac return non_contiguous_segment_ids and drop every span, degrading to GLOBAL. F D2, high severity, LATENT: no context in dac's evaluated set triggers either path (X section 1d). dattn recovers the true span in all three, which is why reference_spans_equal is false on those rows."
 },
